repositories published beside this one by the same organization
(kira, blade, amflow-cpp), each under
the license of its original authors, and are not part of this repository. BootLoops runs
Kira, FireFly and FORM as separate programs
and does not link them into MIT-licensed code. GPL-licensed sources ship
in this repository: tools/subtropica/src/lr_refine.jl and its test (derived from
HyperInt by Erik Panzer; GPL-3.0-or-later; see tools/subtropica/NOTICE for what
that means for the SubTropica module), tools/eichler/genus2/mestre_port.py (a
sympy translation of SageMath's mestre.py and invariants.py by Florian Bouyer,
Marco Streng and Nick Alexander) and tools/eichler/genus2/conic_fast.py (which
carries six statements of the same mestre.py), both GPL-2.0-or-later (see
tools/eichler/NOTICE for what that means for eichler.genus2), and
tools/formglue/form_hyper.py (whose
HyperFORM driver template follows the example drivers shipped with HyperFORM
v1.0 by Adam Kardos, Sven-Olaf Moch and Oliver Schnetz; GPL-3.0-only, as
HyperFORM's own license states, with no later-version option; see
tools/formglue/NOTICE for what that means for formglue). Five more files follow
or copy GPL code of the engines themselves and are GPL-3.0-or-later:
tools/winnow/ibplapper/adapters/user_system.py and
tools/kira-stack/parallel_kira_gen.py and parallel_kira_gen_uds.py (after the
